# One line ending, everywhere.
#
# Git was handing this checkout CRLF on Windows while CI read LF, so code that
# read a file — the exclusions twin parser, the stylesheets inlined into every
# route page — behaved differently on the machine the human walks from than in
# the pipeline. Two gates were green in CI and red here before this line
# (2026-09-10). Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every
# platform; the parsers stay defensive, but they no longer carry the product
# alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The structure check writes this file with LF; named on its own so a run
# never reads as a change with no diff, whatever the line above becomes.
docs/spine/structure.json text eol=lf
# The file is generated, so no hand resolves it: a merge keeps this side's
# copy, and the structure command is rerun on the merged tree. A fresh clone
# sets the `ours` driver once with `git config merge.ours.driver true`
# (CODING_STANDARDS.md, Commands).
docs/spine/structure.json merge=ours
